 blood pressure (197/128 mmHg)", "Systolic murmur (left upper sternal border) indicating valvular abnormality", "Lower-extremity weak pulses suggesting peripheral vascular compromise"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Mechanical Bowel Obstruction Syndrome", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.4864864864864864, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Chronic duration of GI symptoms is more aligned with adhesions/diverticular disease than with acute mesenteric ischemia, which typically presents more abruptly."], "evidence_against": ["The absence of chest pain or arrhythmias undermines cardiac-related GI explanations (B2), while meal/alcohol triggers are more typical of motility issues (gast…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Cardiac-Related Gastrointestinal Symptoms", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.25, "posterior": 0.2252252252252252, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Hypertensive crisis with a murmur suggests valvular disease (e.g., aortic stenosis), but systemic effects like hypoperfusion are less directly linked to this p…"], "evidence_against": ["The absence of chest pain or arrhythmias undermines cardiac-related GI explanations (B2), while meal/alcohol triggers are more typical of motility issues (gast…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Vascular Ischemic GI Syndrome", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "stat